From k20: a model config without a model key (e.g. known: {engine: OllamaOpenAI}) builds the engine with no model, so the provider default answers; resolve returns the alias and Handler::Router relabels the response with it — the client sees a model that didn't answer. Decide: send the alias name upstream as the model, or report the engine's real/default model (response->model from upstream) instead of relabeling.
